":"brown","kme":0.168055,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.372712,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000119698","entrez_id":["57718"],"uniprot":["Q6NUP7"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a HEAT-like repeat-containing protein. The HEAT repeat is a tandemly repeated, 37-47 amino acid long module occurring in a number of cytoplasmic proteins. Arrays of HEAT repeats form a rod-like helical structure and appear to function as protein-protein interaction surfaces. The repeat-containing region of this protein has some similarity to the constant regulatory domain of the protein phosphatase 2A PR65/A subunit. The encoded protein binds protein serine/threonine phosphatase 4c in the cytoplasm. [provided by RefSeq, Jan 2017].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6NUP7","text":"Putative regulatory subunit of serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 4."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}